/WebVella.ERP.sln.ide
/WebVella.ERP.Site/Pages/WV/Pages
**/Properties/launchSettings.json
/.idea/.idea.WebVella.ERP3/.idea

# Outputs written into the workspace by .github/workflows/security-scan.yml
# (the security gate). Generated at run time; never source content. Every file
# the workflow's "Publish the scan evidence" step uploads is listed here, plus
# the intermediate enumerations the coverage assertions write, and the list must
# stay in step with that workflow: a committed copy of a scan artifact is a
# stale record vouching for commits it never examined, which is precisely the
# evidence-integrity failure the gate exists to prevent. The list is COMPLETE
# against the workflow deliberately - an earlier revision named only three of
# them, so running the gate's commands locally, which is how its baselines are
# re-measured, left the rest as untracked files in the working tree, one of them
# the secret-sweep output.
/all-ca-diagnostics.txt
/analyzer-build.txt
# Review finding GATE-01: the derived, path-free analyzer summary the workflow
# publishes was absent from this list while the raw log it replaced was still on
# it, so running the gate's commands locally - which is how its baselines are
# re-measured - left this one file untracked in the working tree and inviting a
# commit. The raw name is kept alongside it because the intermediate log is still
# written when the analyzer build is run by hand.
/analyzer-build-summary.txt
# The commit-bound evidence manifest, for the same reason as every artifact here:
# a committed copy would state a commit and a set of digests it did not measure.
/evidence-manifest.txt
/declared-non-members.txt
/history-exposure-commits.txt
/editorconfig-items.txt
/extra-projects.txt
/manual-verification-matrix.txt
/negative-control.txt
/positive-control.txt
/secret-sweep.txt
/security-allowlist.txt
/security-diagnostics.txt
/security-rule-ids.txt
/security-unreviewed.txt
/sln-members.txt
/startup-smoke.txt
/tracked-projects.txt
/vulnerable-packages.txt
/vulnerable-packages-extra.txt
/vulnerable-packages-wasm.txt
# Scratch directories the Gate 1 positive control and the Gate 2 negative
# control build in; each removes its own on exit, so these only ever appear if
# a run was interrupted.
/.gate-analyzer-control/
/.gate-negative-control/
# The shared failure-log redactor the gate writes and sources. It is generated by
# a workflow step rather than committed, for the same reason as the artifacts
# above: a committed copy could drift from the step that self-tests it, and a
# redactor that is stale is a redactor that leaks.
/.gate-redact.sh
# Deliberately NOT ignored: manual-verification-results.txt. That file is an
# operator-supplied attestation for the manual rows of Gate 5 rather than job
# output, and it MUST be committed for its attestations to count: Gate 5 refuses
# an attestation file that is untracked or locally modified, because reading one
# would restore the "drop a file on the runner and everything passes" path the
# binding exists to remove. Ignoring it here would make every attestation in it
# untrusted by construction. Do not "complete" the list above with it.
